WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.227
Ella was getting ready for Christmas with her family.

2
00:00:05.228 --> 00:00:09.464
She was stringing brightly colored beads with her brother, Danny.

3
00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:20.379
"Guess what?" Grandma called from the kitchen, where she was baking cookies. "It’s snowing!"

4
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:26.158
Howls of delight came from the children as they raced to look out the window.

5
00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:32.219
"It’s going to be a white Christmas after all!" cried Ella.

6
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.225
"Hey, look who’s here!"

7
00:00:34.226 --> 00:00:36.943
said Danny, as Dad entered the room.

8
00:00:36.944 --> 00:00:41.123
He was covered with snow, holding up a tree.

9
00:00:41.124 --> 00:00:46.943
"Now who is going to help me decorate this?" Dad asked with a grin.

10
00:00:46.944 --> 00:00:52.741
Just then, Mom came downstairs carrying a big box of Christmas decorations.

11
00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:57.000
"I think we’re going to need these," she said.

12
00:00:57.001 --> 00:01:02.145
Soon, everyone was in the spirit, helping to decorate the tree.

13
00:01:02.146 --> 00:01:05.984
"It looks beautiful!" said Ella.

14
00:01:05.985 --> 00:01:14.310
"Yes, I agree," Grandma said, "but I think it’s missing something extra special."

15
00:01:14.311 --> 00:01:18.619
"Like what, Grandma?" asked Ella.

16
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:24.189
"Well, I’ve got some old ornaments, from when I was a little girl.

17
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:30.122
I’ve been saving them to share with you, and I think the time has come."

18
00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:33.767
Then she brought out a very old-looking box.

19
00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:38.265
"In here are my treasures from Christmas past.

20
00:01:38.266 --> 00:01:43.151
I have a story to tell about each ornament."

21
00:01:43.152 --> 00:01:47.530
Everyone excitedly gathered around Grandma as she began.

22
00:01:47.531 --> 00:01:55.706
"I remember the first time I walked into my hometown department store during Christmastime.

23
00:01:55.707 --> 00:02:05.270
I was amazed at the beautiful display trees, all different sizes and colors, all brightly lit.

24
00:02:05.271 --> 00:02:09.882
I felt as if I were in a magical fairyland.

25
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:15.825
My mother asked me to help her pick out some ornaments for our tree.

26
00:02:15.826 --> 00:02:17.955
I picked out these,"

27
00:02:17.956 --> 00:02:21.744
said Grandma as she held up two golden balls.

28
00:02:21.745 --> 00:02:24.674
She twirled them between her fingers.

29
00:02:24.675 --> 00:02:29.288
"I still love the way they sparkle."

30
00:02:29.289 --> 00:02:34.993
"They look like little twinkling stars," said Ella admiringly.

31
00:02:34.994 --> 00:02:38.253
"And here’s my sweet little angel,"

32
00:02:38.254 --> 00:02:41.410
said Grandma, reaching into the box.

33
00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:45.891
"My grandfather gave me this one Christmas.

34
00:02:45.892 --> 00:02:50.936
I thought it was the most beautiful thing I’d ever seen.

35
00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.791
See her little wings?

36
00:02:53.792 --> 00:02:57.954
I asked my grandfather if she could fly.

37
00:02:57.955 --> 00:03:05.231
He said, ‘Yes, but only at night when we’re asleep.’" Grandma chuckled.

38
00:03:05.232 --> 00:03:12.600
"So I would sneak downstairs in the middle of the night, trying to catch her flying.

39
00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:19.038
I never did see her flying, but sometimes in my dreams I did!"

40
00:03:19.039 --> 00:03:26.019
Ella laughed. "So you did see her fly! What’s next?"

41
00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.756
"Now this one . . ."

42
00:03:28.757 --> 00:03:32.660
Grandma held up a blue dog with a bone in its mouth.

43
00:03:32.661 --> 00:03:36.472
"My favorite teacher gave me this.

44
00:03:36.473 --> 00:03:41.750
She was always making things and giving them to her students.

45
00:03:41.751 --> 00:03:54.711
Look at the way she painted the dog’s face, and on the back, she painted her name, Mrs. Beatty, and the year, 1944."

46
00:03:54.712 --> 00:03:57.070
Ella looked thoughtful.

47
00:03:57.071 --> 00:04:01.302
"Your ornaments really are treasures, Grandma.

48
00:04:01.303 --> 00:04:04.347
How can you give them up?"

49
00:04:04.348 --> 00:04:09.938
"Because I know you will treasure them as much as I do.

50
00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:12.982
Now this is the last ornament.

51
00:04:12.983 --> 00:04:18.000
I made this when I was in kindergarten.

52
00:04:18.001 --> 00:04:30.007
I remember how carefully I made it, gluing the wooden sticks together, letting the glue dry, then painting the whole thing white.

53
00:04:30.008 --> 00:04:34.639
It’s held up pretty well all these years, I must say."

54
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.842
Grandma held the snowflake ornament in front of the window.

55
00:04:38.843 --> 00:04:43.214
Snow was falling gently outside.

56
00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:45.754
Ella suddenly spoke up.

57
00:04:45.755 --> 00:04:48.158
"I have an idea!

58
00:04:48.159 --> 00:04:52.041
Why don’t we make our own ornaments?"

59
00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:56.111
"That’s a wonderful idea, Ella," said Dad.

60
00:04:56.112 --> 00:04:59.790
"But how are we going to make them?"

61
00:04:59.791 --> 00:05:05.258
"I know a recipe for making clay ornaments," said Grandma.

62
00:05:05.259 --> 00:05:10.138
"All we need is some flour, salt, and water.

63
00:05:10.139 --> 00:05:16.744
Then we cut the clay into shapes, bake our ornaments, and paint them."

64
00:05:16.745 --> 00:05:20.322
So everyone got busy making ornaments.

65
00:05:20.323 --> 00:05:27.711
Dad made a car, Mom made a shoe, Danny made a football, and Grandma made a gingerbread man.

66
00:05:27.712 --> 00:05:34.197
Ella took the longest, but when she was finished, she surprised everyone.

67
00:05:34.198 --> 00:05:41.795
"This is for you, Grandma," said Ella, "because you gave us your special ornaments."

68
00:05:41.796 --> 00:05:51.264
Ella made a snowflake with wings, put gold sparkles on it, and on the back, she had painted "Ella 2008."

69
00:05:51.265 --> 00:05:54.916
Grandma was moved to tears.

70
00:05:54.917 --> 00:06:02.141
"Ella, this is the most beautiful Christmas ornament I’ve ever had.

71
00:06:02.142 --> 00:06:05.854
I will treasure it forever."

72
00:06:05.855 --> 00:06:08.944
Ella gave Grandma a big hug.

73
00:06:08.945 --> 00:06:14.427
"And we will always treasure yours."

